---
const values = [
  ['01', 'Executive-level technical judgment', 'Architecture and trade-off decisions made by someone accountable for them before.'],
  ['02', 'Hands-on delivery', 'The engineer who scopes your project is the one who writes it.'],
  ['03', 'Production engineering experience', 'Systems that run unattended, recover from failure, and can be maintained by your team.'],
  ['04', 'AI agent architecture', 'Tool design, approval gates, evals, and run observability — not a prompt in a loop.'],
  ['05', 'Reliability, testing, security', 'Test coverage and a security pass are in scope, not an upsell.'],
  ['06', 'Direct collaboration', 'One channel, no account layer, straight answers about what’s hard.'],
];
---
<section id="about" class="section-rule">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why SmashGlass</p>
      <h2>A studio built around senior judgement.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          SmashGlass is a boutique engineering studio, not an agency. There is no bench, no junior
          team, and no account layer between you and the people writing your software. The engineer
          who scopes the work is the engineer who builds it.
        </p>
        <p>
          We pair executive-level architecture experience with AI-assisted delivery. That
          combination is the whole proposition: AI makes implementation fast enough to quote a
          fixed price, and senior judgement decides what gets built, where the security boundary
          goes, and which integration will quietly break under load.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our background is engineering leadership and hands-on delivery in production systems
          &mdash; automotive aftermarket platforms, systems integration, and modernization work
          where being wrong is expensive. We take on projects where that experience is the point.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="vals">
        {values.map(([i, t, s]) => (
          <div class="val">
            <span class="i">{i}</span>
            <div>
              <dt class="t">{t}</dt>
              <dd class="s">{s}</dd>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(30px, 5vw, 60px); align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; } }

  .prose { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
  .prose p { color: var(--color-mute); line-height: 1.65; }

  .vals { display: flex; flex-direction: column; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule); margin: 0; }
  .val {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 26px 1fr; gap: 14px;
    padding: 15px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule); align-items: start;
  }
  .val .i { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.64rem; color: var(--color-mute-2); padding-top: 2px; }
  .val .t { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--color-bone); font-weight: 500; }
  .val .s { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--color-mute); line-height: 1.5; margin: 3px 0 0; }
</style>
